From 1ea6b5a720b11f24554d8aef27b4bd024a75f4ad Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: leozhang <zwj8727@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 11 Nov 2026 21:34:36 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] k27: piano-boot-guard=SECS: the installed system's boot
 guarded by the Gunyah watchdog (restart reason bootloader until healthy)

Booted from the ESP (no piano-reset-after), nothing armed the Gunyah watchdog: a hang in the boot (one seen in the GPU bring-up)
left the tablet stuck until power + volume-down. piano-boot-guard=SECS (nothing changes without it):

- EARLY_BOOT: the PMIC SDAM restart reason bootloader (0057's byte) and the watchdog held (32 s bite), pinged every 10 s by a
  thread call. Each tick also sends every other running CPU a nop IPI and checks that its interrupt count moved since the tick
  before: a CPU quiet for two ticks (masked, stalled on the bus) ends the pings and the guard resets through PSCI
  (piano-boot-guard-cpus=0 skips the check). So a hang, a stuck CPU or a panic restart in the boot lands in ABL fastboot.
- At SECS of uptime, in that thread call: healthy when the exec of piano-boot-guard-exec (launchd unless given; "none": the
  uptime alone) has been seen. Healthy: the restart reason back to normal, the pings and checks go on, so a later hang restarts
  the installed system. Not healthy: a PSCI reset into ABL fastboot.
- piano-reset-after set: the guard stays off (0056 keeps the watchdog and the reason); piano-reset-to=bootloader without it keeps
  the reason at bootloader after health.
- The watchdog has one owner now (machine_routines.c piano_watchdog_hold/release/ping/enabled): 0056, the guard and 0062's
  suspend path are its holders and the last one out disables it, so the end of 0062's wake window no longer turns off a watchdog
  the guard holds, and 0062's loop pings it whoever holds it (piano-sleep-wdt=0 included).
- Tests: piano-boot-guard-ping=0 (armed, never pinged: the bite must land in ABL fastboot), piano-boot-guard-test=hang-at=N
  (every CPU masked at N s: before SECS ABL fastboot, after it the installed system).
- machdep.piano_boot_guard (string): armed/healthy, the restart reason, the milestone, the watchdog's holders, pings.
- The decisions are osfmk/arm64/piano_guard_policy.h = UniXNU-piano tooling/k27/piano-guard/piano_guard_policy.h (host-tested).
- 0057's restart reason write checks its read-back; the line names the writer.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
